---
import Layout from "../layouts/ContentPage.astro";
---

<style lang="scss">
	.x {
		position: absolute;
		color: transparent;
		direction: ltr;
	}
	.k {
		float: left;
		direction: ltr;
		top: -999px;
		left: -999px;

		&::after {
			content: "\202e w+tca";
			direction: rtl;
		}
	}
	.r {
		float: right;
		direction: ltr;

		&::after {
			content: "y.net";
			top: -999px;
			left: -999px;
		}
	}
	.r.k::after {
		content: "me";
	}
	.r.k:not(.x) {
		position: absolute;
		color: transparent;
	}
	.rhombus {
		display: inline-block;
		user-select: none;

		direction: rtl;
		unicode-bidi: bidi-override;
	}
</style>
<Layout
	title="About Me"
	description="Info about myself and contact methods"
	pubDate={null!}
	enableComments={false}
>
	<p>
		Yo, waddup.
		<br />
		My name is Fabian, but online I mainly go by the name "Fasguy".
	</p>

	<p>
		I'm a software developer by trade and work on different kinds of
		projects privately. From the simplest tools to WebApps and mods.
	</p>

	<p>
		My main areas of expertise are <code>C#</code> and
		<code>HTML/CSS/JS</code>.
		<br />
		Occasionally I also work with <code>PHP</code>, <code>Java</code>,
		<code>Lua</code>, <code>C++</code> (mainly Arduino) and others.
	</p>

	<p>
		I've also worked with various Game Engines over the years.
		<br />
		<code>Unity</code> and <code>Godot</code> are the most notable examples,
		with <code>Godot</code> being my current main interest.
		<br />
		Depending on how much the definition of "game engine" is stretched, I'd also
		include <code>Garry's Mod</code> (or <code>Source Engine</code>, if you
		want to be pedantic) on that list.
	</p>

	<p>
		My most well known projects are probably my
		<a href="/post/baldis-basics-mod-menu">Mod Menu for Baldi's Basics</a>
		and my <a href="/post/minecraft-toolbox">Minecraft Toolbox</a>.
	</p>

	<p>
		Apart from software development, I also occasionally dabble in different
		areas entirely.
		<br />
		- I make some videos for YouTube, though nowadays that happens very rarely.
		<br />
		- Some of my earliest (still available) published projects are edits of official
		Counter-Strike: Global Offensive maps to turn them into Hide & Seek maps.
		<br />
		- The urge to get properly into 3D modelling has been strong over the years.
		<br />
		<br />
		In conclusion, I just like to try new things every now and then.
	</p>

	<h2 id="contact">Where to find me & contact methods</h2>

	<p>
		YouTube: <a href="https://youtube.com/@Fasguy">@Fasguy</a>
		<br />
		GitHub: <a href="https://github.com/Fasguy">@Fasguy</a>
		<br />
		BlueSky: <a href="https://bsky.app/profile/fasguy.net">@fasguy.net</a>
		<br />
		Steam: <a href="https://steamcommunity.com/id/fasguy">Fasguy</a>
		<br />
		GameBanana: <a href="https://gamebanana.com/members/1651913">Fasguy</a>
		<br />
		E-Mail: <span class="rhombus"
			><span class="r">sgu<span class="r k">me</span></span>af@et<span
				class="k x">cruton</span
			>is<span class="x">william</span>be<span class="k">cont</span></span
		>
	</p>
</Layout>
